225
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
the application will start the UV fill for the entire UV picture.

226
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:16,000
If you need to fill in multiple UV pictures for different types of panels or other purposes,

227
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:20,000
you can select the required panels in the UV editor,

228
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
and then click Use to fill them in.

229
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
After completing the UV fill,

230
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
press the exit key to return to the Airwell window.

231
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
The back-up texture is a function

232
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
that can generate stickers for high-quality objects,

233
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
and then show the optimization function of the multi-layer grid.

234
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
The optimization function of the multi-layer grid

235
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
can also be used in the application.

236
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,000
When the application is successfully implemented,

237
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
the 3D object of the optimization function of the grid is highlighted.

238
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
By using the back-up texture function,

239
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
high-quality textures similar to high-quality models can be implemented,

240
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
but the size of the file is smaller,

241
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:57,000
which will bring more efficient work flow and resource use.

242
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,000
By using the back-up texture of Airwell,

243
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
we can only use the optimized low-quality model

244
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
to generate details,

245
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
and the environment light to guide the stickers,

246
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
instead of creating high-quality models alone.

247
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Detailed hair line stickers are a kind of texture stickers,

248
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
which help to show the surface details of high-quality models in a more three-dimensional way,

249
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
without the need to increase the number of cross-sectional grid.

250
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
It does this by conveying detailed surface information,

251
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
without the need for an extra number of cross-sectional.

252
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:32,000
The environment light block sticker is used to show the gray texture texture.

253
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:37,000
By tracking the light, it highlights the shadow area on the 3D model surface.

254
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Highlighting the darker areas indicates that less lighting is received in this area,

255
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,000
and the brighter areas indicate that the surface lighting is good.

256
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:52,000
The sticker increases the sense of reality by predicting the effect of indirect lighting in the simulated environment.

257
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Choose the detailed hair line sticker and the environment light block sticker in the back window.

258
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:04,000
You can adjust the sun number set by the environment light block sticker to set the number of light lines calculated by each pixel.

259
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
The larger the number, the better the quality of the result.

260
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
However, the calculation time will increase.

261
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Click on the application to generate a sticker.

262
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:17,000
After the application is completed, a new icon will appear on the right side of each sticker option.

263
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
First, click on Preview.

264
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:23,000
You can see the sticker that can be simulated in the 3D window.

265
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Below each sticker, you can enter the intensity value or adjust the slider to change the details to find the intensity of the sticker.

266
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
The default value is 100.

267
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:36,000
You can set it from 0 to the maximum value of 200.

268
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Next to the preview, there is a trash can icon that allows you to delete the sticker.

269
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:51,000
In the material list, you can copy or create a new material and apply the required material to the selected version.

270
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Initially, the material was created according to the number of UV frames.

271
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:59,000
You can right-click on the material to rename or delete the material.

272
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Click on the new add-on to add new materials.

273
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:05,000
You can click on copy and copy the selected material.

274
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,000
And by clicking on the application, the previously created material will be applied to the version.

275
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:16,000
The delete button can delete the material and only delete the unused material.

276
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,000
You can click on the upload button to upload your work.

277
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
The costume will be uploaded to Connect.

278
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
You can also download it from it.

279
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Please note that if you are not satisfied with the upload conditions, it will display warning information and you will not be able to upload the file.

280
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Successful upload must meet four conditions.

281
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:39,000
First, the virtual model, including the joints, must appear in the 3D window.

282
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Second, all versions must be binded to Google.

283
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Third, all UVs must be filled in.

284
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Each UV is located in one frame.

285
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Finally, there must be a detailed drawing of the back.

286
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:58,000
To ensure that all conditions are met, click on the upload at the bottom of the AirReveal window.

287
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
The FBX setting window will appear.

288
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
The default setting is as follows.

289
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
If you have a specific setting,

290
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
please set the option and confirm it.

291
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,000
After connecting to the Connect upload page,

292
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
when the 3D window on the project page is converted and completed,

293
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:18,000
you can download the FBX and download the costume FBX files.

294
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:24,000
You can also check the transformed costumes in the AirReveal in the Connect page.

295
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:31,000
In addition, you can download the ZPRJ and FBX files from the list of the project.

296
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
After all the work is done,

297
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
close the AirReveal window.

298
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:38,000
If you need to save the progress in the middle

299
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
or want to use the file for further work,

300
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,000
you can save it as a project file in Cloud.

301
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,000
It is the same as the standard file saving method.

302
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
The file is saved as a project file.

303
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,000
All the information applied in the AirReveal window

304
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:57,000
