00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,000
Input

483
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Input

484
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:17,000
The shirt panel that is 100% larger will create a pink line on the outside of the panel.

485
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:25,000
If the panel does not change the shrink rate, even if the shrink rate is turned on, the pink line will not appear.

486
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Next, I will explain the optimization of the 3D function and the application of the symmetrical panel.

487
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:39,000
In this version, the simulation can be applied to the symmetrical panel to quickly complete the same shape left and right.

488
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:43,000
In the 3D window, select the panel that needs to be copied to the simulation form.

489
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:49,000
After selecting the panel, right-click and select the application of the symmetrical panel form.

490
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:56,000
This function can retain the existing shrink line and apply the simulation form to the symmetrical panel.

491
00:28:56,000 --> 00:29:03,000
If the panel is not set to symmetrical, when selecting the application of the symmetrical panel form, a warning message will appear.

492
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:06,000
It shows that some selected panels are not set to symmetrical.

493
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:09,000
The application of the symmetrical panel form can only be applied to the 3D model.

494
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:13,000
This function can only be applied to the symmetrical panel of the 3D model.

495
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:17,000
Next, I will explain the optimization of the functional optimization of the 3D model.

496
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Display the 3D model to try on and wear the suit.

497
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
In the previous version, it is difficult to check through the naked eye whether the 3D model is wearing the suit.

498
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:30,000
From this version, the function has been updated.

499
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
You can check by opening and closing the display of the 3D model to try on and wear the suit.

500
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,000
First, I applied the 3D model to try on and wear the suit before opening.

501
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:42,000
In the previous version, I applied the 3D model to try on and wear the suit.

502
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:47,000
In the 3D window, the digital menu bar shows the 3D model.

503
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Click on the 3D model to try on and wear the suit icon.

504
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Then you can see the 3D model to try on and wear the suit.

505
00:29:55,000 --> 00:30:01,000
If you want to hide the 3D model, click on the icon to try on and wear the suit.

506
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:05,000
Next is the improvement related to materials.

507
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:08,000
First, I added the multidirectional grid optimization function.

508
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:12,000
In the previous version, I mentioned multidirectional grid optimization in the Everywhere section.

509
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Next, let's take a closer look at this function.

510
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
In the work, if the file is too large and requires the size of a slightly optimized high-quality copy,

511
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:25,000
including the copy, the button, and the pull-head, the pull-head, and the index,

512
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:29,000
you can use the multidirectional grid optimization tool added in the corresponding attribute editor

513
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:33,000
to help you easily store and use your copy files.

514
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,000
In order to check whether the 3D model is wearing the suit, click on the icon to try on and wear the suit.

515
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
In order to check whether the 3D model is wearing the suit,

516
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:44,000
click on the icon to try on and wear the suit.

517
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:50,000
When you click on the corresponding button, the button, the pull-head, the pull-head, and the index,

518
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:55,000
you will see a multidirectional grid optimization tool at the bottom of the attribute editor.

519
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Click on the download menu on the right side of the multidirectional grid optimization tool.

520
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:01,000
You can see two types.

521
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:03,000
One is the default mesh grid type.

522
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:07,000
And the other is the bare-board flat type.

523
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:12,000
Mesh grid type is a method to optimize objects by reducing the number of grid lines.

524
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:19,000
And the bare-board flat type can be optimized by shaping objects into flat images.

525
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:22,000
First, select the Mesh grid type.

526
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:25,000
At this time, a count technology will appear at the bottom.

527
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:31,000
The input value will show the number of multidirectional grid lines of the object.

528
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,000
If the number is changed to 5000,

529
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:37,000
you can see that the number of grid lines of the object in the 3D window is reduced.

530
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:40,000
If the number of multidirectional grid lines is too low here,

531
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:42,000
for example, lower than 800,

532
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:47,000
there will be a larger change in the final appearance and a lower quality.

533
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:49,000
On the other hand, we input 50,000.

534
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:53,000
You can see that the maximum grid number that can be applied is the grid number of the original file.

535
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,000
It cannot exceed the number.

536
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:59,000
In addition, it should be noted that the current multidirectional grid optimization function

537
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:03,000
can only be applied to button, copy, pull head, pull piece, and straight button.

538
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:06,000
It cannot be applied to the line.

539
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:10,000
Next, we will change the type to the bare-board flat type.

540
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:13,000
At this time, the 3D object will become a flat image.

541
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:21,000
If you want to reduce the size of the file, you can try using this option.

542
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Next is the optimization related to the sticker.

543
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:28,000
In the new version, you can set the rotation angle of each color sticker

544
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,000
in order to optimize it.

545
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:31,000
And when the sticker is out of the version,

546
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:35,000
the original shape of the sticker will be displayed.

547
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:40,000
First, let's take a look at how to set the rotation angle of different colors.

548
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:44,000
In the main menu bar, find the editor Color Open,

549
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:48,000
and we will check the changes in different colors.

550
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Then click the adjustment sticker tool in the 2D or 3D tool bar to select the sticker.

551
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:56,000
You can see that in the right mouse button editor,

552
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:58,000
under the sticker change message,

553
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:03,000
we have added the function of linking all the colors.

554
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Here, by using the function of linking all the colors,

555
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:11,000
you can set the rotation angle of each color separately.

556
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:13,000
Select the sticker and rotate it,

557
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:16,000
then click the update button in the color window.

558
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:19,000
You can see that the sticker rotates only in color A,

559
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:23,000
and the rest of the colors remain the same.

560
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:27,000
Next, let's take a look at when the sticker is out of the version.

561
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:30,000
The original shape of the sticker is displayed.

562
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:32,000
In the previous version,

563
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:34,000
when the sticker is applied to the 2D version,

564
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:38,000
the sticker is set to be visible only in the area of the 2D version.

565
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:40,000
When the sticker position is set,

566
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:42,000
the area outside the sticker is not visible,

567
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:47,000
so it is very inconvenient to continuously move the sticker for inspection.

568
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:53,000
Now it has been improved to check the image of the sticker even outside the 2D version.

569
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:55,000
Next, go back to the 2D window,

570
00:33:55,000 --> 00:34:00,000
and move the sticker to the position where it is related to the outside of the version.

571
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,000
You can see that the sticker is not only displayed in the 2D version,

572
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:06,000
but also visible outside.

573
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,000
And only by using the adjustment sticker tool,

574
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,000
you can select the sticker in the 2D window or 3D window,

575
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:14,000
so that it can display all,

576
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:17,000
otherwise the sticker is not visible in the part outside the version.

577
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Through the improved function,

578
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:23,000
we can rotate the sticker and check the sticker in different colors more easily.

579
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:24,000
In addition,

580
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:28,000
we have added the option of adding and deleting all unused items.

581
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:30,000
In the new version,

582
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:35,000
the items that are not assigned and unused in the 3D window can be deleted at once.

583
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:40,000
This option can be used for all object objects in the 3D window.

584
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:44,000
For example, let's see the button in the 3D window.

585
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:48,000
You can see that there are four buttons in these buttons that have not been used,

586
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:50,000
and two of them are applied to the costume.

587
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:52,000
On the unused button,

588
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,000
click on the button on the right,

589
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:59,000
and select the button to delete all unused buttons from the list.

590
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:02,000
You can see that the unused items will be deleted.

591
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:08,000
This can help us to manage unused items more effectively.

592
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:10,000
Next is the update about rendering.

593
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,000
In the new version,

594
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
we added the option of controlling the size of the round top in the skylight attribute.

595
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:20,000
We can find the round top parameters of the skylight in the rendering light setting,

596
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:27,000
by adjusting the size of the round top light to adapt the scene.

597
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:30,000
First, open the light line attribute in the rendering window,

598
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:35,000
and open the round top size.

599
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:38,000
This makes a gap in the background when moving the camera.

600
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:41,000
When you need to direct the light pattern to the ground,

601
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:45,000
this is very useful.

602
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:47,000
The round top control is basically made up of three parts,

603
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:49,000
the bottom of the hemisphere,

604
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:50,000
the ground,

605
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:54,000
and the transition area between the two.

606
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:56,000
First is the radius parameter.

607
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:57,000
As the value increases,

608
00:35:57,000 --> 00:36:00,000
the radius of the whole round top becomes wider.

609
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:02,000
The smallest value is 1 meter.

610
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:04,000
When the value is set to the smallest value,

611
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:06,000
you can see that the radius of the light also becomes narrower.

612
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,000
At this time,

613
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:11,000
you can see that the upper end of the virtual model and the costume are not lighted.

614
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:15,000
Here the default value is 4 meters.

615
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Next is the ground projection height.

616
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,000
If you increase the value,

617
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,000
you will see that the image of the ground surface at the bottom

618
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:24,000
will rise to the top of the hemisphere.

619
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,000
Accordingly,

620
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:28,000
the projection value of the light will also change.

621
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,000
Therefore,

622
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:33,000
you can see that the light reflected on the virtual model will also change.

623
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:37,000
Here the default value is 1 meter.

624
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,000
Finally,

625
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:40,000
it is the ground mixing option.

626
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:41,000
If you increase the value,

627
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,000
you will see that the ground surface at the bottom

628
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:46,000
and the hemisphere top will be roundly mixed together,

629
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:48,000
and the shape of the transition area will change.

630
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Here the default value is 0.5.

631
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:59,000
If you want to save the original size of the change,

632
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:03,000
you can save all the optical properties as vrp files,

633
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:07,000
or click on the file storage in the top left-hand column

634
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:12,000
to save all the rendering properties as zvrp files.

635
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Next is about the update and improvement of the animation.

636
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,000
In the new version,

637
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:23,000
it is more convenient to edit the animation frame and the selection in the animation.

638
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,000
First,

639
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,000
in the new version,

640
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:28,000
it is more convenient to adjust the frame rate in the animation.

641
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:31,000
When we stop the mouse at the end of the slide at the bottom,

642
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:33,000
it will display in the blue color.

643
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Drag the slide can manually control the frame rate of the animation slide.

644
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:41,000
You can also enlarge the specific frame rate you want in the timeline

645
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:45,000
to edit the key frame.

646
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:49,000
If you want to display the entire animation frame in the timeline,

647
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:51,000
you can double-click the slide bar at the bottom,

648
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:56,000
or click the button on the far right of the bottom to adjust the animation frame range.

649
00:37:56,000 --> 00:38:00,000
The smallest and largest frames displayed on the timeline and the change area

650
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:03,000
will be set to the same number of frames for the entire animation frame,

651
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:06,000
so that you can check all the frames at once.

652
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:13,000
In addition, when you export the costume file with the animation as an elembic file,

653
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:18,000
you can use the current frame option to only export a single frame.

654
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:19,000
First,

655
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,000
on the timeline,

656
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:23,000
place the playhead to the frame you want to extract,

657
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:29,000
or enter the corresponding value directly in the current frame.

658
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Then,

659
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:31,000
in the main menu,

660
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,000
find the file,

661
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,000
export,

662
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:38,000
elembic og awa.

663
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:40,000
In the export elembic window,

664
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:42,000
select the animation menu,

665
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:45,000
and select the current frame option.

666
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:46,000
In this way,

667
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:48,000
only one frame will be exported,

668
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:51,000
and all other animation data will be deleted.

